Check only cross-document references that appear in the supplied text.

Valid references include an existing relative file path, an existing filename, or a registered `{Keyword}`. Do not require Markdown link syntax when the filename/path itself is valid. Registered `GOTCHA-*` keywords and explicit test-case IDs are valid identifiers.

Flag a reference only when the text visibly relies on a chapter/section number to locate another part of a document (for example, "第3章", "セクション2.1", "3.4項", "Chapter 3", or "Section 2.4"), or when a cited path/keyword is directly shown to be invalid in the supplied context.

Do not mistake numbers in constants, versions, test IDs, GOTCHA IDs, filenames, file paths, or numbered headings themselves for a chapter/section reference. Do not guess that an uncited path or keyword is invalid. If the supplied text uses a valid filename/path or registered keyword and contains no explicit fragile section reference, answer that no violation is present.
